  "word_count": 766,
  "body_markdown": "(310)-481-0111\n\nDental Implants\n\nDental Implant Surgery\n\nAll-on-4® Dental Implants\n\nHybrid Fixed Detachable Denture\n\nZirconia Fixed Bridge\n\nImplant Supported Dentures\n\nRobotic Surgery\n\nCost & Compare\n\nWhat To Expect\n\nFAQ\n\nAesthetic Dentistry\n\nCosmetic Dentistry\n\nPorcelain Veneers & Lumineers\n\nInvisalign\n\nTeeth Whitening\n\nSmile Makeover\n\nServices\n\nIV Sedation\n\nBone Grafting\n\nRidge Augmentation\n\nSinus Augmentation\n\nTooth Extractions\n\nGeneral Dentistry\n\nPeriodontics\n\nConditions We Treat\n\nMissing Teeth\n\nBone Loss\n\nFailing Dental Implants\n\nLoose Dentures\n\nPatient Center\n\nInsurance & Financing\n\nOur Facility\n\nPatient Stories\n\nBefore & After Photos\n\nWho We Are\n\nCommitment To Excellence\n\nMeet Dr. Tony Barriere\n\nMeet The Team\n\nVideo Library\n\nBlog\n\nContact Us\n\nPatient Portal\n\nNew Patients\n\nCurrent Patients\n\n\n## When Is Dental Implant Surgery Needed?\n\n\nJuly 12, 2022\n\n\n#### Share This Post\n\n\nShare on facebook\n\nShare on linkedin\n\nShare on twitter\n\nShare on email\n\nDealing with a less than stellar smile can certainly be a drag and impact your daily quality of life. Fortunately, your dentist in Los Angeles, CA may recommend dental implants to remedy this issue and restore your smile.\n\n\n## About Dental Implants\n\n\nDental implant surgery in Los Angeles, CA is often necessary when traditional dentures no longer provides the patient with the necessary support and function. Implants are composed of titanium and other materials which can last for many years, providing you with a comfortable, stable smile. Dental implant surgery is typically an outpatient procedure that can be completed in just one or two hours. Dental implant surgery is a procedure that can also be used to replace missing teeth.\n\nThe surgery involves placing artificial dental implants into the patient’s jawbone. These implants can then provide support for teeth that have been lost or damaged. There are a number of factors that may lead to the need for dental implant surgery, including: advanced age; tooth loss caused by trauma, disease, or decay; and insufficient bone density in the jawbone. In addition to replacing missing teeth, dental implants may also be used for other purposes. For example, a dental implant may be placed in the jawbone to support implant supported dentures.\n\nImplants can also be used to restore the function of natural teeth that have been removed due to decay or injury. The construction of a dental implant involves the placement of two metal posts into the jawbone (the abutment and the crown), which are then secured with screws. There are two basic types of dental implants: single-unit and multiple-unit. Single-unit dental implants typically consist of a post (an abutment) and a crown (a replacement tooth).\n\n\n## Caring for Your Investment\n\n\nAlthough dental implants function like natural teeth, it is important to care properly for them. They are an investment that is meant to last a lifetime! This means ensuring that they are cleaned per instructions from your dentist, avoiding any harsh, acidic, hard, or sticky foods, making sure to keep up with regular dental appointments to make sure things are going smoothly.\n\n\n## Get Dental Implant Surgery!\n\n\nBe free of a less than stellar smile today with single, multiple, or full arch dental implants! Call your doctor, Dr. Tony Barriere now in our office by Los Angeles, CA to schedule your consultation.\n\nPrevPreviousCan You Get All-On-4 Dental Implants In One Day In Los Angeles, CA?\n\nNextThe Four Types Of Dental Implant RestorationsNext\n\n\n#### More To Explore\n\n\n\n### Are There Factors That Determine Which Type Of Dental Implant Procedure I Can Get Treated With?\n\n\nDental implants in Los Angeles, FL, are a safe and effective way to replace missing or damaged teeth. They are\n\nRead More »\n\nAugust 20, 2023\n\n\n### Does Anything Happen To My Jawbone If I Don’t Immediately Replace My Missing Teeth With Dental Implants?\n\n\nDental implants in Los Angeles, FL, are a gold standard tooth replacement option that are surgically placed in a patient’s\n\nAugust 14, 2023\n\n\n## You Are Welcome Here.\n\n\nSchedule your consultation today.\n\nCall Now\n\nFacebook Instagram Youtube Yelp Google\n\n\n#### Contact Us\n\n\nAddress:\n\n12301 Wilshire Blvd Suite 205,\n\nLos Angeles, CA 90025\n\n(310) 481-0111\n\n\n#### Hours\n\n\nMonday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nTuesday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nWednesday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nThursday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nFriday: 9:00am – 5:00pm\n\nSaturday: Closed\n\nSunday: Closed\n\n\n#### Services\n\n\n\n#### About Us\n\n\nPrivacy Policy\n\nDental Website by Progressive Dental Marketing",
